  "aiReview": {
    "strengths": {
      "bestArea": "Finishing at the rim (career 47.9% FG on 263 attempts, up to 54.4% in 2025-26) and knocking down open catch-and-shoot threes (41.5% FG career on unguarded looks)",
      "bestPlayType": "Transition (career 1.012 PPP on 250 possessions, the most efficient of his high-volume actions, trending up each season: 0.926 → 0.916 → 1.180, graded Very Good by 2025-26)",
      "overallStrength": "A downhill, live-dribble guard who finishes efficiently around the rim and gets more efficient the faster the game moves — his transition offense has climbed from Below Average to Very Good over three seasons while also taking on a bigger share of his possessions (18.6% → 24.9%)."
    },
    "weaknesses": {
      "worstArea": "Pull-up/dribble jump shooting — his single highest-volume shot type by far (321 career attempts, more than any other category) and consistently his least efficient (32.7% career FG, 0.760 PPS, in the 30-36% FG range every season)",
      "worstPlayType": "P&R Ball Handler — his largest role by a wide margin (34.3% of career possessions) but only average efficiency (0.753 career PPP) that has plateaued below his freshman-year mark (0.783 → 0.737 → 0.746)",
      "overallWeakness": "The shape of his shot diet works against him: the play type he leans on most (P&R Ball Handler) has never regained his freshman efficiency, and the shot type he takes most often (the pull-up jumper) is his least accurate. Neither is a small-sample blip — both are backed by 300+ possessions/attempts across three seasons.",
      "developmentTarget": "Tighten up pick-and-roll shot selection and finishing as the ball handler, and lean less on the pull-up dribble jumper relative to his more efficient reads (transition, spot-up, and finishing at the rim). Worth a film check too: his guarded vs. unguarded catch-and-shoot splits flipped in 2025-26 (guarded graded Excellent, unguarded Below Average) after two seasons of the opposite pattern — not enough on its own to call a trend, but worth watching."
    }
  },
